WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:04.210
The characters that are still alive for the
final chapter of Game of Thrones have gone

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:08.720
through some monumental personal evolutions,
but no character has had quite as shocking

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.669
a transformation as Bran Stark, whose metamorphosis
into the Three-Eyed Raven rendered him more

00:00:13.669 --> 00:00:16.800
cryptic than ever at the start of Game of
Thrones season 8.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.480
A peculiar line Bran uttered during the season
premiere struck viewers as incredibly odd,

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.380
and people are debating its true meaning.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.260
"What are you doing out here?"

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.860
"Waiting for an old friend."

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:32.610
The final moments of the Thrones season 8
premiere seemed to confirm that the not-so-dear

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.700
pal he was anticipating meeting again was
Jaime Lannister.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.260
Way back in the first episode, Jaime shoved
Bran out of a Winterfell tower window when

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.600
Bran caught him and Cersei in the heat of
passion.

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:46.899
When the two spotted one another from opposite
ends of the Winterfell courtyard in the present,

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:50.550
it marked the first time they had laid eyes
on each other since the incident that left

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.340
Bran paralyzed.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.720
It seemed he sprinkled in some signature Stark
sass in sarcastically calling Jaime an "old

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:56.220
friend."

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.800
But some Game of Thrones fans have a different
idea about what Bran's comment truly meant.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.800
One theory suggests that Bran wasn't talking
about Jaime Lannister at all.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.650
Instead, Bran may have been referring to another
man whom he hasn't seen in years, who also

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.220
betrayed him and his family: Theon Greyjoy.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.400
Once he rescues his sister, Yara, from their
uncle Euron, Theon admits that he doesn't

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.930
want to go back to the Iron Islands and hold
strong.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.940
It would be simple to wait out the war between
the White Walkers and the humans of Westeros

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:25.990
on a land that the monsters can't reach, but
Theon has other plans: he wants to head to

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:28.440
Winterfell, where Theon was a ward to Ned
Stark.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.640
Theon wants to fight alongside the Starks,
his second family.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.920
"You want to go to Winterfell, to fight for
the Starks.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:39.720
Go."

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.100
Theon is absolutely an old friend of the Stark
family.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.520
Theon ultimately bit the hand that fed him,
however, turning his back on Robb Stark during

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.420
the War of the Five Kings and taking his father
Balon Greyjoy's side to carry out an invasion

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.020
of the North.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.940
Things were made even worse when Theon tricked
the people of Winterfell into thinking he

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.230
burned Bran and his younger brother Rickon
alive after the Greyjoys seized control of

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:01.940
the castle.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.920
Theon's betrayal sent him on a terrifying
journey, which saw him become the tormented

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.940
servant-slash-pet of Ramsay Bolton before
escaping by the skin of his teeth.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:13.280
It's little wonder that now, after having
gone through everything he did following his

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.200
double-crossing of the Starks, Theon would
want to right his wrongs with the Starks.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.760
In the Game of Thrones season 8 trailer, Bran
is heard welcoming someone home.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:28.240
"Everything you did brought you where you
are now, where you belong."

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.780
Vanity Fair notes that it sounds like Bran
is speaking of Winterfell.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:36.700
While that line could be delivered to Sansa,
Arya or Jon, those three are already at Winterfell

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.960
and feel safe there.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.040
Theon, on the other hand, he has struggled
to find his place in the world for many years,

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.260
and it sure would mean a lot hear that he
can call Winterfell home again.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:49.220
Theon may be taking his final step toward
redemption and his imminent meeting with Bran

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.660
could be what seals the deal.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:55.100
Theon already has forgiveness from Jon, who
told him during the season 7 finale that he

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:59.690
is just as much a Stark as he is a Greyjoy,
but receiving absolution from Bran would mean

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:00.340
that much more.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.800
Then again, maybe there's no connection between
what Bran says in the Thrones season 8 trailer

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.140
and his "old friend" line.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:10.140
Bran isn't the person he used to be and has
been saying all kinds of strange stuff since

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.600
he became the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.200
For example, when Jon hugs him and tells him
he's a man now, Bran replies:

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.240
"You’re a man now!”

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.060
“Almost."

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.580
Is he just being cryptic for the sake of it?

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.940
Is he talking about being in a wheelchair,
and how that may cause some to think less

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:28.440
of him?

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.840
Or does he mean he's something other than
totally human because he's the Three-Eyed

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:32.440
Raven?

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:36.220
Everything that comes out of Bran's mouth
can be interpreted a thousand different ways.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.020
His comment about waiting for an old friend
is no exception.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.430
With only five episodes of Game of Thrones
remaining, fans will hopefully find out the

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.920
truth about Bran's cryptic line soon enough.

